---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe1540.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Cash and Cash Equivalents" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Three Activity Classifications" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. THE GENUINE CHOICE — Direct or Indirect Method, Freely Elected" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Classifying Interest and Dividends" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Dividends Paid and Charged to Retained Earnings" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Non-Cash Transactions" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — the Indirect Method" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Worked Example — the Direct Method for the Same Facts" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Relationship to IAS 7 — and Contrast With ASBE's Mandatory Direct Method" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "16. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Presenting cash inflows and outflows by activity, with genuine method flexibility</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1540 governs the PREPARATION of the CASH Flow STATEMENT — CLASSIFYING an ENTERPRISE'S cash INFLOWS and OUTFLOWS into OPERATING, INVESTING, and FINANCING activities. UNLIKE the MANDATORY direct-METHOD-plus-reconciliation APPROACH we SAW under ASBE No. 31 (see the COMPANION Chinese GAAP poster), ASPE offers a GENUINELY free CHOICE between the DIRECT and INDIRECT method, WITH no SUPPLEMENTARY reconciliation REQUIRED regardless of WHICH method is CHOSEN (Section 5).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The fourth required primary statement</div><div class="principle">This Section applies TO the PREPARATION of the CASH Flow STATEMENT — the FOURTH required PRIMARY statement COMPRISING a COMPLETE set of ASPE financial STATEMENTS, PRESENTING the ENTERPRISE'S cash INFLOWS and OUTFLOWS during THE period.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Cash and Cash Equivalents</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Short-term, highly liquid investments</div><div class="text-supporting">CASH equivalents ARE short-TERM, highly LIQUID investments READILY convertible TO known AMOUNTS of CASH, subject TO an INSIGNIFICANT risk OF changes IN value — SUBSTANTIALLY the SAME definition USED internationally UNDER IAS 7.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Three Activity Classifications</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Operating, investing, and financing</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Operating activities</span><span>PRINCIPAL revenue-PRODUCING activities and OTHER activities THAT are NOT investing or FINANCING</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Investing activities</span><span>ACQUISITION and DISPOSAL of LONG-term assets and OTHER investments NOT considered CASH equivalents</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Financing activities</span><span>ACTIVITIES changing the SIZE and COMPOSITION of the ENTERPRISE'S owners' EQUITY and BORROWINGS</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE GENUINE CHOICE — Direct or Indirect Method, Freely Elected</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">No mandatory supplementary reconciliation, unlike ASBE</div><div class="text-supporting">ASPE ALLOWS an ENTERPRISE to PRESENT operating CASH flows using EITHER the DIRECT method (PRESENTING major CLASSES of GROSS cash RECEIPTS and PAYMENTS) OR the INDIRECT method (STARTING from NET income, ADJUSTING for non-CASH items and WORKING capital CHANGES) — a GENUINE, unrestricted CHOICE, with NO supplementary RECONCILIATION mandated REGARDLESS of WHICH method IS selected. THIS mirrors IAS 7'S OWN flexible APPROACH internationally, and STANDS in GENUINE contrast to ASBE No. 31 (see the COMPANION Chinese GAAP poster), WHICH requires the DIRECT method PLUS a MANDATORY supplementary INDIRECT-method reconciliation.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Classifying Interest and Dividends</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Reasonable flexibility, consistently applied</div><div class="text-supporting">INTEREST and DIVIDENDS received OR paid are CLASSIFIED as OPERATING, investing, OR financing activities, DEPENDING on THEIR nature — an ENTERPRISE selects a CONSISTENT classification and APPLIES it FROM period to PERIOD, DISCLOSING the POLICY chosen PER Section 1505.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Dividends Paid and Charged to Retained Earnings</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Presented separately as financing outflows</div><div class="text-supporting">DIVIDENDS PAID and CHARGED to RETAINED earnings are PRESENTED SEPARATELY as CASH flows USED in FINANCING activities — SIMILARLY, cash FLOWS relating TO dividends PAID by SUBSIDIARIES to NON-controlling interests ARE presented SEPARATELY as CASH flows USED in FINANCING activities.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Non-Cash Transactions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Excluded from the statement, disclosed separately</div><div class="text-supporting">SIGNIFICANT investing and FINANCING transactions that do NOT involve CASH or CASH equivalents (e.g. ACQUIRING an ASSET through a DIRECTLY related LEASE, or ISSUING shares TO settle a LIABILITY) are EXCLUDED from the CASH Flow STATEMENT itself, but DISCLOSED separately ELSEWHERE in the FINANCIAL statements.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — the Indirect Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Starting from net income, adjusting for non-cash items</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Reconciling net income to operating cash flow</div><div class="wk-body">A private company reports net income of $850,000, depreciation of $120,000, and a $60,000 increase in accounts receivable during the year.</div><div class="wk-answer">Using the INDIRECT method, NET cash from OPERATING activities = $850,000 + $120,000 − $60,000 = <strong>$910,000</strong>, presented AS a SINGLE, complete STATEMENT — WITH no FURTHER direct-method DISCLOSURE required.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — the Direct Method for the Same Facts</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">An equally acceptable alternative presentation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Presenting gross cash receipts and payments instead</div><div class="wk-body">The same company, choosing the direct method instead, determines cash received from customers of $9,400,000 and cash paid to suppliers and employees of $8,490,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">Using the DIRECT method, NET cash from OPERATING activities = $9,400,000 − $8,490,000 = <strong>$910,000</strong> — the SAME final RESULT as the INDIRECT method, PRESENTED differently, WITH BOTH approaches EQUALLY acceptable under ASPE and NEITHER requiring the OTHER as a SUPPLEMENT.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1540 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Cash flows classified by operating, investing, and financing activities</span><span>Policy for classifying interest and dividends, applied consistently</span><span>Significant non-cash investing and financing transactions</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Classifying a specific cash flow among operating, investing, or financing activities</span><span>Whether to use the direct or indirect method</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this is primarily a classification and presentation standard</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 7 — and Contrast With ASBE's Mandatory Direct Method</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 1540 vs IAS 7 vs ASBE No. 31</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1540</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 7</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Method choice</span><span>Free choice, direct or indirect</span><span>Free choice — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Supplementary reconciliation required</span><span>NO</span><span>NO — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">ASPE and IAS 7 are THOROUGHLY converged HERE — BOTH stand IN genuine CONTRAST to ASBE No. 31'S OWN mandatory DIRECT method PLUS required SUPPLEMENTARY reconciliation (see the COMPANION Chinese GAAP poster), a USEFUL illustration of HOW even TWO broadly CONVERGENT frameworks (ASPE and IFRS) can DIVERGE from a THIRD (ASBE) on the SAME underlying TOPIC.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every cash flow event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Cash inflows/outflows</span><span><span class="badge scf">SCF</span></span><span>Classified by operating, investing, or financing activity</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1400</span><span>General Standards of Financial Statement Presentation — supplies the general presentation framework this Section's cash flow requirements sit within</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Direct method</div><div class="glossary-def">A Cash Flow Statement presentation showing major classes of gross cash receipts and payments, freely electable under ASPE.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Indirect method</div><div class="glossary-def">A reconciliation starting from net income, adjusting for non-cash items, an equally acceptable alternative under ASPE with no supplementary requirement.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe1540 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
